    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During the Woodland period, the Mahican people settled the Pownal area, while others, such as the Mohawks, traveled across it.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pownal%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early European settlers in Pownal may have arrived in the 1730s, possibly as Dutch tenants of the Manor of Rensselaerswyck.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pownal%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pownal residents were deeply divided during the American Revolution between those loyal to the colonies and those sympathetic to England.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pownal%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Some residents of Pownal joined the Green Mountain Boys under Ethan Allen due to land conflicts between New Hampshire and New York.",
